WEBVTT

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.037
A design is made of objects.

00:00:06.037 --> 00:00:15.360
In this video you put them in the right order, copy, mirror and colour them, on a pair of cherries.

00:00:16.467 --> 00:00:19.201
I open my drawing as an SVG.

00:00:19.201 --> 00:00:27.307
Every shape becomes an object, stitched in the order in which the file paints them.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:34.729
On the right are the colours, the first at the top, the last at the bottom.

00:00:34.729 --> 00:00:38.694
The arrow opens a colour and shows its objects.

00:00:38.694 --> 00:00:46.120
The Object panel tells you at which place it is stitched and how many others it lies on.

00:00:47.233 --> 00:00:52.764
The cherry lies on two objects, the stem and the highlight.

00:00:52.764 --> 00:00:56.420
That is because white comes before red.

00:00:56.420 --> 00:01:02.513
I drag white below red in the list, and there are the highlights.

00:01:02.513 --> 00:01:05.793
What is stitched later lies on top.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:12.003
The card above offers to leave out the cherries under the highlights.

00:01:12.003 --> 00:01:14.740
Then there is no double thread there.

00:01:15.833 --> 00:01:18.823
Now the leaf gets a partner.

00:01:18.823 --> 00:01:23.520
A right click opens a small menu: Duplicate.

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:28.324
The same buttons are in the Object panel too.

00:01:28.324 --> 00:01:31.633
I mirror the copy horizontally.

00:01:32.733 --> 00:01:35.665
Then I drag it to the left.

00:01:35.665 --> 00:01:41.853
The thin line shows it snaps exactly onto the first leaf.

00:01:42.967 --> 00:01:46.536
The second leaf gets a darker green.

00:01:46.536 --> 00:01:50.602
Click the colour square, choose a thread.

00:01:50.602 --> 00:01:54.767
It is stitched right after the first leaf.

00:01:55.867 --> 00:02:05.027
The space bar shows you the order: stems, leaves, cherries and, last of all, the highlights.

00:02:06.133 --> 00:02:10.659
Realistic threads show you how it looks on the fabric.

00:02:10.659 --> 00:02:13.173
Your pair of cherries is done.
